# Glossary

> **Drop this into the root of any project where you want a domain
> glossary that AI agents read before assuming what a term means.**
> `/glossary-init` does this automatically with candidates surfaced
> from your code. Edit the entries below; the marker comment on the
> first line is load-bearing — keep it.

Domain terms specific to *this* repo. Hand-curated. Update via
`/glossary-init --add <term>` or by editing this file directly.

**Read this before assuming a term means what it does elsewhere** —
domain vocabulary diverges between projects. A `Lead` in a CRM is not
a `Lead` in journalism, even if both ship as a Python class named
`Lead`.

## Conventions

- One entry per term, H2 heading = the term as it appears in code.
- 1–2 sentence definition. State what it **is** and what distinguishes
  it from similar terms.
- Optional bullet list: `Aliases` (other names this concept has),
  `Code` (1–3 representative paths).
- Entries sorted alphabetically by term (case-insensitive).
- If you need a term for one team-internal concept, define it here. If
  you need many terms for cross-cutting concepts, consider a
  `docs/conventions/` subdirectory and link from this file.

---

## Account

A billing entity. One Account → one or more Tenants. Holds payment
method, billing address, and tax ID. Distinct from `Tenant` (which is
the *operational* unit, not the billing unit).

- Aliases: billing-account
- Code: `src/billing/account.py`, `src/billing/account_test.py`

## Invoice

A finalized billing document sent to an Account at the end of a billing
cycle. Distinct from `Charge` (one-off card transaction) and `LineItem`
(component of an Invoice). An Invoice may contain LineItems from
multiple Tenants on the same Account.

- Code: `src/billing/invoice.py`

## Lead

In this repo: a **journalist's article lead** — the opening paragraph
of a story. Distinct from CRM "Lead" (sales prospect), which we do not
have a concept for here. If you see `Lead` in code, assume it's an
article lead unless explicitly named otherwise (e.g. `SalesLead`).

- Aliases: article-lead, story-lead, opener
- Code: `src/content/lead.py`

## Tenant

A customer organization — the operational unit of multi-tenancy. One
Tenant → many Users; one Account (billing) → one or more Tenants. We
isolate Tenant data at the database row level (every table has
`tenant_id`); see [ADR 0007](docs/adr/0007-tenant-row-isolation.md) for
why row-level instead of schema-per-tenant.

- Aliases: org, organization, workspace
- Code: `src/auth/tenant.py`, `src/billing/account.py`

